{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,26]],"date-time":"2026-10-26T04:34:50Z","timestamp":1792989290092,"version":"4.5.0"},"reference-count":38,"publisher":"Wiley","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,25]],"date-time":"2026-10-25T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1792886400000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/"},{"start":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,25]],"date-time":"2026-10-25T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1792886400000},"content-version":"tdm","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/doi.wiley.com\/10.1002\/tdm_license_1.1"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/100000001","name":"National Science Foundation","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["R01EB023607"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["R01EB023607"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/100000001","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/100000001","name":"National Science Foundation","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["R01AI194917"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["R01AI194917"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/100000001","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]},{"DOI":"10.13039\/100000001","name":"National Science Foundation","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","award":["U01CA269147"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["U01CA269147"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/100000001","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"publisher"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":["advanced.onlinelibrary.wiley.com"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"short-container-title":["Advanced Science"],"abstract":"<jats:title>ABSTRACT<\/jats:title>\n                  <jats:p>\n                    CRISPR\u2013Cas12a molecular diagnostics rely on target\u2010activated collateral cleavage of single\u2010stranded DNA (ssDNA) reporters to generate fluorescence signals, yet the mechanisms governing reporter substrate processing remain poorly understood. Here we show that Cas12a\n                    <jats:italic>trans<\/jats:italic>\n                    \u2010cleavage involves both endonucleolytic cleavage and exonucleolytic trimming. We further demonstrate that terminal phosphate modification of ssDNA substrates accelerates substrate cleavage activity and modulates\n                    <jats:italic>trans<\/jats:italic>\n                    \u2010cleavage kinetics, thereby enhancing fluorescence output. Guided by this mechanistic insight, we engineered fluorophore\u2013quencher ssDNA reporters bearing terminal phosphate modifications and identified a 3\u2032\u2010phosphate\u2010engineered reporter that enables faster signal generation and higher fluorescence intensity. Incorporation of the engineered reporter into the CRISPR\u2013Cas12a system enabled the development of Phos\u2010CRISPR (\n                    <jats:bold>Phos<\/jats:bold>\n                    phate\u2010engineered DNA reporters boost\n                    <jats:bold>CRISPR<\/jats:bold>\n                    ), a rapid, sensitive, and specific nucleic acid detection platform that achieves results within 20\u00a0min, approximately threefold faster than conventional CRISPR assays. Applied to herpes simplex virus 1 detection, the Phos\u2010CRISPR combined with recombinase polymerase amplification achieved a limit of detection of 20 aM and accurately identified clinical swab samples. These findings provide a general framework for understanding Cas12a\n                    <jats:italic>trans<\/jats:italic>\n                    \u2010cleavage activity and establish a mechanistically informed strategy for enhancing next\u2010generation CRISPR diagnostics.\n                  <\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1002\/advs.78445","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2026,10,26]],"date-time":"2026-10-26T04:08:03Z","timestamp":1792987683000},"update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1002\/crossmark_policy","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Phosphate\u2010Engineered DNA Reporters Boost CRISPR\u2010Cas12a\n                    <i>Trans<\/i>\n                    \u2010Cleavage for Rapid and Sensitive Nucleic Acid Detection"],"prefix":"10.1002","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0003-5839-1059","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Rui","family":"Yang","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Biomedical Engineering University of Connecticut Health Center  Farmington Connecticut USA"},{"name":"Department of Biomedical Engineering University of Connecticut  Storrs Connecticut USA"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Chong","family":"Guo","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Biomedical Engineering University of Connecticut Health Center  Farmington Connecticut USA"},{"name":"Department of Biomedical Engineering University of Connecticut  Storrs Connecticut USA"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-5753-114X","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Minjie","family":"Pei","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Biomedical Engineering University of Connecticut Health Center  Farmington Connecticut USA"},{"name":"Department of Biomedical Engineering University of Connecticut  Storrs Connecticut USA"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-9725-1345","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Jiongyu","family":"Zhang","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Biomedical Engineering University of Connecticut Health Center  Farmington Connecticut USA"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0009-0002-0878-3778","authenticated-orcid":false,"given":"Xin","family":"Guan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Biomedical Engineering University of Connecticut Health Center  Farmington Connecticut USA"},{"name":"Department of Biomedical Engineering University of Connecticut  Storrs Connecticut USA"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"